  "seed": 1,
  "notes": "1907 four-storey Edwardian flats over a continuous run of shopfronts; pale warm-grey stucco, twelve 3-sided bays on storeys 2-4, two steel fire escapes, tall ground storey with a divided transom band, flat parapet with a thin cornice. Shopfront run held 2.2 m clear of both acute wedge corners (frame returns poked through the flank edges). Cool pale-grey and off-white painted stucco per unit (four flats fronts, wallZones), crisp white trim and window heads, bays 0.6 m deep with moulded white crowns, brackets and frieze panels (kit bayCrown), a separate cornice per unit (kit corniceZones), cream shop piers with dark red-brown trim pilasters and a red-brown fascia band, dark tiled bulkheads, dark red-brown shop frames, a deep blue awning pair over the widest shop at the north-west end, two fire escapes (middle and four-fifths from the south-east end) with stringers, balusters and a drop ladder (kit fireEscapes), dark room tones and drawn blinds behind the sashes (glassBacking), cafe fit-out on the ground storey. Four flats read as separate buildings - zone lines moved onto the piers (0.236/0.486/0.736) with projecting seam strips, parapets stepped per flat (0 / 0.45 / 0.2 / 0.5 m) with their cornices and paired brackets, crisp painted finish instead of the speckled stucco; six shop tenancies (cbShopUnits) with their own frame colours, blank fascia sign bands, window graphics, a small tricolour flag, green-framed shop with an orange door, navy scalloped awning pair; shop fit-outs with dark back walls (no see-through to the rear); storeys 3.7 m + 3 x 2.85 m with taller sashes (0.6-2.45 m); curtains and sheers per window; heavier fire escapes (continuous stringers, knee braces, kick plates, stowed ladder); upper flats along the front, one room per bay, fit-out differing per room and storey.",
